## Narrative

This round is a build task. It changes no code, no test, and no file under `content/`. HEAD was
`440a64dc` (= the role base), and the Green code `23f746a4` is inside `440a64dc~6..HEAD`.

The Thai filter ran first and printed `0` for each part 7 script that this round copies, for the
part 7 log, and for the plan. Every capture ran through `light_capture_2_9g.py` or
`heavy_capture_2_9g.py` of part 7, and each capture prints its dropped-line count. The 3 heavy jobs
ran in the foreground with a 1800 s, 600 s, or 1200 s limit.

STEP 1 (the pictures). `link_pictures_2_9i.py` made 29 hard links with 29 equal SHA-256 pairs and 29
the same inode. The student front keeps
`9087de2811caed07c6f3c7c75a0fffe4a52f7e99b03b1fbd094e5b55ebe3881f`. `fix-back-edge-2-9i.py` writes
the back `881e93b2a87385eb15e5cf0240df8629c501a10f0375284f9cec2fe09eda37c4` from the unchanged source
`5411e37ec7044d7afd70726ee5fffeccd985225ef0b0da4283db8e6a3979b7bf`, with
`DIFFERING_PIXELS_OUTSIDE_STRIP 0` and `EDGE_FILL_OK True`. `prep-teacher-front-2-9i.mjs` writes the
prepared teacher front `0901411875407c09bd69e779f5aad31b36147d84d0e742feee6316712bf96283`, with
`RAW_EQUAL true` and `PREP_OK true`. Each new script is a copy of its part 7 partner with 3 exact
replacements (`numstat 4 4`).

STEP 2 (the build). One heavy run exits 0 on the first attempt. It prints `Covers of Level 2 Unit 1
set 1: 32 pages, 44 files` and 4 lines `All checks pass.` (`build-2-9i.txt`).

STEP 3 (the reader files). `copy_readers_2_9i.py` replaces the 34 files of `readers-a3/` and
`readers-leaf/`. Each old SHA-256 equals its line of the old MANIFEST before the write.
`REPLACED 34`, `PAIR_EQUAL 34`, `COPY_OK true`.

STEP 4 (the r4 book files). `copy_2_9i.py` writes the 10 r4 book files as byte copies: `COPIES 10`,
`SHA_PAIRS_EQUAL 10`, `GUARDS_OK 10`. The guard set is the 8 part 7 print files plus the 2 r3 print
files, so the r2, r3, r5, and old `-alt-hlogo` files stay untouched. The 2 information lines show
that the r4 back PNGs equal the r3 back PNGs (`9f5b588f...` and `ad6c3335...`), so G4 holds.

STEP 5 (page 12). Both heavy builds exit 0: `--a3-color` gives 2 A3 files of 12 pages, and
`--workbook` gives 1 PDF/X file of 12 pages. `page12_2_9i.py` renders page 12 of the hello A3 file
(4963x3508 px, `13cbdfd3...`) and the page-12 leaf of Nan Can Nod (2479x3508 px, `7fe62a54...`).
The ink coverage of the workbook file is C, M, and Y at 0.00000 on each of the 12 pages.

The first run stopped at `PAGE12_OK false`. The counts were `words_in_this_book=1`,
`storytime_advantage=1`, `sprout=0` on the A3 page 12, and `1`, `2`, `1` on the workbook page 7.
The cause is the reader template, not the fix: the A4 workbook leaf holds page 12 (the word list)
and page 1 (the reader cover of the print_r1 template) on one sheet, and page 1 prints the band word.
The logo SVG holds no text element, so the series text on page 12 comes from the reader back page.

The orchestrator decided on 2026-11-11: the band word must be 0 on page 12 only, and the series line
is information everywhere. The corrected rule reads the 2 halves of the leaf page with
`pdftotext -x 0 -y Y -W 596 -H 421`. The workbook leaf holds page 12 and page 1; the page 12 rule
reads the page 12 half; page 1 of the print_r1 reader template still prints the band word, outside
this fix. The A3 page 12 gives phrase 1 and band 0. The workbook page 7 gives TOP (page 1) phrase 0
and band 1, and BOTTOM (page 12) phrase 1 and band 0. The rule `with-nan-can-nod` chose page 7. The
old build of 2026-11-11 (6 pages) holds the phrase on page 3 with the band word 2 times on the whole
page, and the new build holds it 1 time. `PAGE12_OK true`.

STEP 6 (the sheets). `contact-2-9i.py` runs in one heavy run (600 s) and gives `CONTACT_OK true`. It
replaces `readers-a3.png`, `readers-leaf.png`, and `all.png`, and each old SHA-256 equals its
MANIFEST line before the write. It creates `student-alt-hlogo-r4.png` and
`teacher-alt-hlogo-r4.png`, each 2064x1496 px.

STEP 7 (the MANIFEST). `manifest_check_2_9i.py` rewrites `MANIFEST.txt` in the part 7 format. The new
file holds 114 lines with SHA-256
`1ff3dfd361c66ee2e334826cd0da489adff137cdee85f00ddaa8d7b3ddc0a384`. It holds 60 byte-equal lines
(the 48 lines of part 7 and the 12 r3 lines of part 7), 37 changed lines (the 34 reader files and the
3 sheets), and 17 new lines (the 10 r4 book files, the 2 r4 sheets, and the 5 files of
`reader-back-r4/`). `sha256sum -c` on the 2-column projection gives 114 OK and 0 FAILED.
`MANIFEST_OK true`. The first run held `UNCHANGED_LINES 48` unchanged lines and stopped at
`UNCHANGED_LINES_EXPECTED false`; the 12 r3 lines stay in the folder, so the count is 60. The script
now asserts 60 and the run passes from the saved old copy.

STEP 8 (the final check log). `print_gate_final_2_9i.py` runs in one heavy run (1200 s) and writes
`print-gate.txt`. It gives `PASS_LINES=43`, `FAIL_LINES=0`, and `MANIFEST_SHA256_START` equal to
`MANIFEST_SHA256_END` = the new MANIFEST. The 4 book variants (r2 and r4) hold 4 lines
`All checks pass.` each. The new `CHECK_12_READER_BACK` is PASS. Every other check function is
byte-equal: after the 4 added docstring lines and the 79 added code lines of CHECK_12 are removed,
the new script equals the part 8 script with the same replacements applied
(`CHECK_FUNCTIONS_BYTE_EQUAL true`, `numstat 113 29`). So the 4 print-check mutants of part 8
(`MUTANTS_CAUGHT=4`) stay valid.

STEP 9 (the plan). `plan_insert_2_9i.py` inserts 3 lines directly after the last Part 7 sub-line
(`  - Part 7 new files (SHA-256):`, line 207), before Task 2.10: `INSERTED 3`. `git diff --numstat`
prints `3	0`, and the plan Thai count is 0. Task 2.9 stays `[~]`, because Task 2.8 is `[~]`.

STEP 10 (the pages for the PM). The 8 full-size pages and the 5 sheets are in the Part 9 plan line
with their pixel size and SHA-256, and in the handoff of the result block.

STEP 11 (the commits). Commit 1 `37543807` holds the 24 new files of the run folder, the rewritten
`print-gate.txt`, and the plan. Commit 2 holds this log alone.

